{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_9","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"cd /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-14_14-15-46-hashicorp_raft-real-run/draft; python3 - <<'PYEOF'\nimport json\np='update.json'\nd=json.load(open(p))\nd['investigations'].append({\n  \\\"ref\\\": \\\"@verify_overlap_rate\\\",\n  \\\"question\\\": \\\"Across phases, how often does the cut-off leader's confirmation outlive the election of a competing leader when the cluster's nodes do not share timer settings, in contrast to the uniform case where the separation held in every trial?\\\",\n  \\\"source_ids\\\": [\\\"raft_verifyleader_votes\\\",\\\"raft_quorumsize_voters\\\",\\\"replication_notifyall\\\",\\\"config_validate_timer_relations\\\",\\\"raft_follower_election_trigger\\\",\\\"raft_lease_check_counts_voters\\\"],\n  \\\"hypothesis\\\": \\\"Because the ordering between the confirmation window and a competing election follows from the per-node relation between the leader's lease and the voters' election timeout, the mixed configuration should show the overlap in essentially every trial while the uniform one should show none, provided each trial starts from a stable cluster whose timers are reset by the same leader.\\\",\n  \\\"discriminator\\\": \\\"Repeat the mixed-timer trial twenty times and the uniform control twice, each on a fresh cluster, and compare the per-trial boolean that records whether any confirmation followed the appearance of a competing leader. The mixed case is expected to overlap throughout; the controls are expected to show no competing leader during the window.\\\",\n  \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"active\\\",\n  \\\"parent_id\\\": \\\"92e710d02abc4842a2f6c79e3aae70e4-question-0\\\"\n})\nd['experiment']={\n  \\\"investigation_id\\\":\\\"@verify_overlap_rate\\\",\n  \\\"harness_path\\\":\\\"assurance_generated_test.go\\\",\n  \\\"source_ids\\\":[\\\"raft_verifyleader_votes\\\",\\\"raft_quorumsize_voters\\\",\\\"replication_notifyall\\\",\\\"config_validate_timer_relations\\\",\\\"raft_follower_election_trigger\\\",\\\"raft_lease_check_counts_voters\\\"],\n  \\\"scope\\\":{\n    \\\"description\\\":\\\"Twenty-two trials on hand-built four-node clusters, one fresh cluster per trial: twenty with per-node timers (the leader carrying a 50ms heartbeat, election and lease, the other nodes a 10ms heartbeat, 20ms election and 5ms lease) and two with every node on the leader's settings. Each trial forces leadership onto the slow node with a normal transfer, demotes one node to nonvoter, isolates the leader and that nonvoter from the two remaining voters in both directions, then verifies the leader repeatedly while reading whether either isolated node reports Leader.\\\",\n    \\\"assumptions\\\":[\n      \\\"Per-node configurations are accepted by ValidateConfig, which is applied per node, so the mixed case is a legal cluster whose members drifted apart rather than a rejected one.\\\",\n      \\\"Each node is bootstrapped with the same configuration, as the target's own multi-node tests do.\\\",\n      \\\"The leader is forced onto the slow node by a normal LeadershipTransferToServer so the lease under test belongs to the leader.\\\",\n      \\\"Verification is driven through the same channel the exported API uses; a competing leader is detected by reading the two isolated nodes' states.\\\",\n      \\\"Trials start from a stable cluster whose follower timers were just reset by the leader's heartbeats; a partition landing during an already-running election is not part of this basis.\\\",\n      \\\"The dry run is native feedback only; the retained execution is what will be interpreted.\\\"\n    ],\n    \\\"excluded\\\":[\n      \\\"No application read is served; the measured quantity is whether a confirmation coexists with a competing leader, not what a client would receive.\\\",\n      \\\"No on-disk store, no network transport, no multi-process execution.\\\",\n      \\\"Only two timer sets are contrasted; the probe does not sweep configurations.\\\"\n    ],\n    \\\"parameters\\\":{\n      \\\"trials\\\":\\\"20 mixed (trial ids 0-19), 2 uniform controls (trial ids 20-21)\\\",\n      \\\"poll_interval_ms\\\":2,\n      \\\"recorded_operands\\\":\\\"leader_lease_ms, voter_election_ms, voter_election_shorter_than_lease, polls, confirmations, last_confirmation_ms, first_peer_leader_ms, confirmations_after_peer_leader, confirmation_after_peer_leader, leader_stepped_down, leader_term, peer_term, leader_applied_index\\\"\n    }\n  },\n  \\\"prerequisites\\\":[{\\\"alias\\\":\\\"pre\\\",\\\"event\\\":\\\"verify_baseline\\\"}],\n  \\\"comparisons\\\":[\n    {\\\"event\\\":\\\"verify_exposure\\\",\\\"identity_fields\\\":[\\\"trial\\\"],\\\"admission_alias\\\":\\\"pre\\\",\n     \\\"applicability_conditions\\\":[{\\\"field\\\":\\\"voter_election_shorter_than_lease\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":True}],\n     \\\"assertion\\\":{\\\"field\\\":\\\"confirmation_after_peer_leader\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":True},\n     \\\"description\\\":\\\"Every mixed-timer trial shows at least one confirmation after a competing leader exists; any trial without one is reported as a witness, which is what makes the observed rate readable from the outcome.\\\"},\n    {\\\"event\\\":\\\"verify_exposure\\\",\\\"identity_fields\\\":[\\\"trial\\\"],\\\"admission_alias\\\":\\\"pre\\\",\n     \\\"applicability_conditions\\\":[{\\\"field\\\":\\\"voter_election_shorter_than_lease\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":False}],\n     \\\"assertion\\\":{\\\"field\\\":\\\"confirmation_after_peer_leader\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":False},\n     \\\"description\\\":\\\"Control: with every node on the leader's settings no confirmation follows a competing leader.\\\"}\n  ],\n  \\\"prefix\\\":\\\"Unchanged from the single-witness harness apart from repetition: each trial builds four nodes by hand (an in-memory transport each, all pairs connected, one in-memory store serving as both log and stable store, an in-memory snapshot store and a MockFSM), bootstraps each node with the same configuration, starts each with its own Config, waits for any leader, transfers leadership to the slow node and waits until it reports Leader, demotes the fourth node with DemoteVoter, records a healthy baseline verification, applies one command, disconnects the leader and the nonvoter from the two remaining voters in both directions, then polls the verification path every 2ms while the leader still reports Leader and watches the two isolated nodes for a leader, emitting one summary event per trial with the counts, the last confirmation's elapsed time, the first competing leader's elapsed time, how many confirmations followed one, the terms and the configured timer values.\\\"\n}\njson.dump(d,open(p,'w'),indent=2)\nprint('keys',list(d.keys()),'investigations',[i.get('id') or i.get('ref') for i in d['investigations']])\nPYEOF\n/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/.venv/bin/python -I -B -c \\\"import sys; sys.path.insert(0, '/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/src'); from consensus_assurance.cli import main; raise SystemExit(main())\\\" validate --run /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-14_14-15-46-hashicorp_raft-real-run --submission update.json 2>&1 | tail -4\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_9","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"cd /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-14_14-15-46-hashicorp_raft-real-run/draft; python3 - <<'PYEOF'\nimport json\np='update.json'\nd=json.load(open(p))\nd['investigations'].append({\n  \\\"ref\\\": \\\"@verify_overlap_rate\\\",\n  \\\"question\\\": \\\"Across phases, how often does the cut-off leader's confirmation outlive the election of a competing leader when the cluster's nodes do not share timer settings, in contrast to the uniform case where the separation held in every trial?\\\",\n  \\\"source_ids\\\": [\\\"raft_verifyleader_votes\\\",\\\"raft_quorumsize_voters\\\",\\\"replication_notifyall\\\",\\\"config_validate_timer_relations\\\",\\\"raft_follower_election_trigger\\\",\\\"raft_lease_check_counts_voters\\\"],\n  \\\"hypothesis\\\": \\\"Because the ordering between the confirmation window and a competing election follows from the per-node relation between the leader's lease and the voters' election timeout, the mixed configuration should show the overlap in essentially every trial while the uniform one should show none, provided each trial starts from a stable cluster whose timers are reset by the same leader.\\\",\n  \\\"discriminator\\\": \\\"Repeat the mixed-timer trial twenty times and the uniform control twice, each on a fresh cluster, and compare the per-trial boolean that records whether any confirmation followed the appearance of a competing leader. The mixed case is expected to overlap throughout; the controls are expected to show no competing leader during the window.\\\",\n  \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"active\\\",\n  \\\"parent_id\\\": \\\"92e710d02abc4842a2f6c79e3aae70e4-question-0\\\"\n})\nd['experiment']={\n  \\\"investigation_id\\\":\\\"@verify_overlap_rate\\\",\n  \\\"harness_path\\\":\\\"assurance_generated_test.go\\\",\n  \\\"source_ids\\\":[\\\"raft_verifyleader_votes\\\",\\\"raft_quorumsize_voters\\\",\\\"replication_notifyall\\\",\\\"config_validate_timer_relations\\\",\\\"raft_follower_election_trigger\\\",\\\"raft_lease_check_counts_voters\\\"],\n  \\\"scope\\\":{\n    \\\"description\\\":\\\"Twenty-two trials on hand-built four-node clusters, one fresh cluster per trial: twenty with per-node timers (the leader carrying a 50ms heartbeat, election and lease, the other nodes a 10ms heartbeat, 20ms election and 5ms lease) and two with every node on the leader's settings. Each trial forces leadership onto the slow node with a normal transfer, demotes one node to nonvoter, isolates the leader and that nonvoter from the two remaining voters in both directions, then verifies the leader repeatedly while reading whether either isolated node reports Leader.\\\",\n    \\\"assumptions\\\":[\n      \\\"Per-node configurations are accepted by ValidateConfig, which is applied per node, so the mixed case is a legal cluster whose members drifted apart rather than a rejected one.\\\",\n      \\\"Each node is bootstrapped with the same configuration, as the target's own multi-node tests do.\\\",\n      \\\"The leader is forced onto the slow node by a normal LeadershipTransferToServer so the lease under test belongs to the leader.\\\",\n      \\\"Verification is driven through the same channel the exported API uses; a competing leader is detected by reading the two isolated nodes' states.\\\",\n      \\\"Trials start from a stable cluster whose follower timers were just reset by the leader's heartbeats; a partition landing during an already-running election is not part of this basis.\\\",\n      \\\"The dry run is native feedback only; the retained execution is what will be interpreted.\\\"\n    ],\n    \\\"excluded\\\":[\n      \\\"No application read is served; the measured quantity is whether a confirmation coexists with a competing leader, not what a client would receive.\\\",\n      \\\"No on-disk store, no network transport, no multi-process execution.\\\",\n      \\\"Only two timer sets are contrasted; the probe does not sweep configurations.\\\"\n    ],\n    \\\"parameters\\\":{\n      \\\"trials\\\":\\\"20 mixed (trial ids 0-19), 2 uniform controls (trial ids 20-21)\\\",\n      \\\"poll_interval_ms\\\":2,\n      \\\"recorded_operands\\\":\\\"leader_lease_ms, voter_election_ms, voter_election_shorter_than_lease, polls, confirmations, last_confirmation_ms, first_peer_leader_ms, confirmations_after_peer_leader, confirmation_after_peer_leader, leader_stepped_down, leader_term, peer_term, leader_applied_index\\\"\n    }\n  },\n  \\\"prerequisites\\\":[{\\\"alias\\\":\\\"pre\\\",\\\"event\\\":\\\"verify_baseline\\\"}],\n  \\\"comparisons\\\":[\n    {\\\"event\\\":\\\"verify_exposure\\\",\\\"identity_fields\\\":[\\\"trial\\\"],\\\"admission_alias\\\":\\\"pre\\\",\n     \\\"applicability_conditions\\\":[{\\\"field\\\":\\\"voter_election_shorter_than_lease\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":True}],\n     \\\"assertion\\\":{\\\"field\\\":\\\"confirmation_after_peer_leader\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":True},\n     \\\"description\\\":\\\"Every mixed-timer trial shows at least one confirmation after a competing leader exists; any trial without one is reported as a witness, which is what makes the observed rate readable from the outcome.\\\"},\n    {\\\"event\\\":\\\"verify_exposure\\\",\\\"identity_fields\\\":[\\\"trial\\\"],\\\"admission_alias\\\":\\\"pre\\\",\n     \\\"applicability_conditions\\\":[{\\\"field\\\":\\\"voter_election_shorter_than_lease\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":False}],\n     \\\"assertion\\\":{\\\"field\\\":\\\"confirmation_after_peer_leader\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":False},\n     \\\"description\\\":\\\"Control: with every node on the leader's settings no confirmation follows a competing leader.\\\"}\n  ],\n  \\\"prefix\\\":\\\"Unchanged from the single-witness harness apart from repetition: each trial builds four nodes by hand (an in-memory transport each, all pairs connected, one in-memory store serving as both log and stable store, an in-memory snapshot store and a MockFSM), bootstraps each node with the same configuration, starts each with its own Config, waits for any leader, transfers leadership to the slow node and waits until it reports Leader, demotes the fourth node with DemoteVoter, records a healthy baseline verification, applies one command, disconnects the leader and the nonvoter from the two remaining voters in both directions, then polls the verification path every 2ms while the leader still reports Leader and watches the two isolated nodes for a leader, emitting one summary event per trial with the counts, the last confirmation's elapsed time, the first competing leader's elapsed time, how many confirmations followed one, the terms and the configured timer values.\\\"\n}\njson.dump(d,open(p,'w'),indent=2)\nprint('keys',list(d.keys()),'investigations',[i.get('id') or i.get('ref') for i in d['investigations']])\nPYEOF\n/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/.venv/bin/python -I -B -c \\\"import sys; sys.path.insert(0, '/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/src'); from consensus_assurance.cli import main; raise SystemExit(main())\\\" validate --run /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-14_14-15-46-hashicorp_raft-real-run --submission update.json 2>&1 | tail -4\"","aggregated_output":"keys ['rationale', 'investigations', 'interpretations', 'experiment'] investigations ['92e710d02abc4842a2f6c79e3aae70e4-question-0', '@verify_overlap_rate']\n{\"valid\": true, \"run_id\": \"3fe38e261b0c47799f27769cc21c4645\", \"elapsed_seconds\": 3129.8499510629954, \"diagnostics\": [], \"meaning\": \"Read-only validation of these bytes and saved state; no acceptance, execution or budget reservation\", \"no_change\": false, \"execution_requested\": true, \"effects\": [{\"object\": \"investigations\", \"action\": \"update\", \"target\": \"92e710d02abc4842a2f6c79e3aae70e4-question-0\", \"changed_fields\": [\"disposition\", \"resume_conditions\"]}, {\"object\": \"investigations\", \"action\": \"create\", \"target\": \"@verify_overlap_rate\"}, {\"object\": \"interpretations\", \"action\": \"append\", \"target\": \"interpretations[0]\", \"investigation_id\": \"92e710d02abc4842a2f6c79e3aae70e4-question-0\", \"changed_fields\": [\"experiment_id\", \"source_ids\", \"executions\", \"conclusion\", \"defect_claim\", \"rationale\", \"knowledge\", \"counterevidence\", \"limitations\"]}, {\"object\": \"interpretations\", \"action\": \"append\", \"target\": \"interpretations[1]\", \"investigation_id\": \"9af1f08cbbbb45298f90a629cefc3686-question-2\", \"changed_fields\": [\"source_ids\", \"executions\", \"rationale\", \"knowledge\", \"counterevidence\", \"limitations\", \"joint_history\"]}, {\"object\": \"experiments\", \"action\": \"create\", \"target\": \"experiment\"}]}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_10","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"submission\":\"update.json\",\"summary\":\"The mixed-timer receipt decided the point positively and forced a correction: with the leader on a 50ms lease and the other voters on a 20ms election timeout, a competing leader appeared 21ms after the partition and the cut-off leader went on confirming — ten confirmations followed the appearance of a leader one term ahead — while the uniform control saw no competing leader during its confirmation window at all. I therefore corrected the account I had recorded earlier rather than merely extending it. The child question's claim is now asserted for per-node timings and the parent VerifyLeader account is revised with that receipt joined to its own, so the stale-read basis the documented read pattern depends on is witnessed instead of argued — with the honest boundary kept: uniform configurations still close the window first, as twelve earlier trials and the source path show, so the exposure depends on whether a cluster's nodes share their timer settings, an environmental condition the library permits rather than enforces. I cleared the pause on the child question, recorded the knowledge uses at their exact revisions, and kept the counterevidence visible: the overlap needs differing timers, no application read is served so the witness is about the confirmation rather than a delivered value, the competing leader's appearance is only known within the 2ms poll, and the mixed witness was a single trial. Because that last point is the only remaining measurement, I also extended the same probe to twenty mixed trials and two controls in this same submission, declared both branches as comparisons so the observed rate is readable from the outcome either way, and kept it as a new child question about frequency rather than folding it into an answered one; my local dry run of that extension showed the overlap in all twenty mixed trials, with the competing leader appearing between 14ms and 44ms and between two and fifteen confirmations following it, against no overlap in either control.\"}"}}
